    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0609" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">718.1915/758: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-07T10:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                                1926—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:53
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Department’s telegram number 29 dated December 29, 1925, 7 p.m.</p>
                <p>Costa Rica has rejected Fabrega’s counterproposal for rectification of the
                    boundary and his proposal to postpone the negotiations until May.</p>
                <p>I shall forward on January 9 a memorandum on the final conference between
                    President Jiménez and Fabrega.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d322-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
